WEBVTT

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:08.820
Makina's situation has stabilized, but she won't be singing anytime soon.

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:11.240
Makina...

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:13.530
What happened to your hand?

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:17.200
I, uh, hurt it on Windermere.

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:19.310
Is it okay?

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:21.410
Yeah, it's no big deal.

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:25.970
We failed to destroy the Protoculture system

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:28.900
and lost Mikumo Guynemer to the enemy.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:31.660
Her song echoed through the entire galaxy,

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:35.590
surpassing the numbers we've seen so far.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:38.000
Did she become a turncoat?

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.020
No! She'd never do that!

00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:43.050
My apologies, First Lt. Chuck.

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:45.770
But how does she know the song of the wind?

00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:49.670
That was probably the song of the stars.

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:50.690
Of the stars?

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:55.320
The legend says it's the song 
of the Wind Singers' ancestors.

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:59.580
But Mikumo's voice was different from how she usually sounds.

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:02.220
Its color was...

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:04.530
that of darkness.

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:11.950
<i>Our kiss will link us from one end to the other</i>

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:16.380
<i>Our affection is too hot for mere passionate love</i>

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:21.230
<i>We can be in absolute zero</i>

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:36.030
<i>I'll spark a dream in you</i>

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:40.550
<i>I'll embrace all you believe in</i>

00:01:40.550 --> 00:01:43.170
<i>Let your genes go wild</i>

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:50.050
<i>I love you so much, but I try to play it cool sometimes</i>

00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:53.900
<i>Tear off my mask and squeeze me to a whole new dimension</i>

00:01:54.680 --> 00:02:00.870
<i>Our cores crash into each other, confirming our uncovered love</i>

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:05.270
<i>The tears we can't cry on our own connect us to the future</i>

00:02:06.730 --> 00:02:11.890
<i>Our passionate love will shoot us into a super nova-like state</i>

00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:17.780
<i>We can do this! No wounds can hold us back if we're together</i>

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:20.500
<i>Charm me with your passion, pray to the heavens</i>

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:23.870
<i>Our super big bang will breathe life into a new genesis</i>

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:27.130
<i>We burn our lives for this fusion</i>

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:32.610
<i>We are in absolute zero</i>

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:41.590
What's wrong? It's not like you to call us over.

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:43.790
This.

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:45.850
This voice recorder is from the VF-22.

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:49.410
Makina found it and took it.

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:51.480
It was broken and the data was corrupt.

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:53.730
You managed to salvage it?

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:56.130
What do you want to do?

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:01.740
Play it.

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:08.660
Falcon 2. You are off route.

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:11.390
I repeat. You are off route.

00:03:12.490 --> 00:03:13.880
This is Falcon 2.

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:15.160
Dad...

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:17.230
There is strong turbulence.

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:20.020
I will take a longer route to the target.

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:26.040
The satellites show no sign of any 
turbulence. Return to the original route.

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:28.280
That's weird. Please check agai—

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:32.080
No, wait. Two enemy units are headed your way.

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:34.560
Head straight to the royal capital of Darwent.

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:36.790
Is something wrong?

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:38.310
Respond, Falcon 2!

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:39.430
This is an orde—

00:03:41.350 --> 00:03:44.040
Not yet. I'm still too close.

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:50.730
It switched to remote control.

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:53.360
The dimensional weapon was already being readied.

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:54.960
Remote control?

00:03:55.950 --> 00:03:58.890
Guess I won't be able to keep my promise to come home.

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:01.560
Sorry, Asahi.

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:02.700
Mom...

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:05.470
Hayate...

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:16.140
So he pretended to obey his orders

00:04:16.140 --> 00:04:18.630
and went in a direction where it'd do the least damage...

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:21.880
He was trying to protect the civilians.

00:04:22.670 --> 00:04:27.480
But why would they detonate it off target?

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:32.040
I figure they feared Captain Wright would get captured and leak intel.

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:35.760
Or perhaps they just wanted to blame it all on him.

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:41.460
But I've never heard the call sign "Falcon 2" before.

00:04:41.730 --> 00:04:43.840
There was other non-audio data too.

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:47.480
Protoculture ruins?!

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:49.050
Where did Hayate's dad...

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:52.440
Seems like he was a special agent.

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:58.650
Seven years ago, NUNS had already begun investigating if those ruins could serve as some ultimate weapon.

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:01.390
Fearing that others might unlock the mystery before them...

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:03.460
They fired off a dimensional weapon...

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:06.560
A spy, huh?

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:10.740
Your old man was quite the guy.

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:17.180
Captain.

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:17.790
Hm?

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:20.260
A shuttle is requesting docking permission.

00:05:20.260 --> 00:05:21.540
A shuttle?

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:32.860
I was told you are here to discuss Mikumo Guynemer.

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:33.930
Indeed.

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:40.560
She is the Star Singer.

00:05:42.310 --> 00:05:46.130
Isn't the Star Singer just some legend?

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:47.520
Far from it.

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:48.530
There is no mistake.

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:51.170
But why was she in Walküre?

00:05:51.170 --> 00:05:53.740
The Earthlings revived her.

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:58.280
Seven years ago, a NUNS special agent found a genetic fragment

00:05:58.280 --> 00:06:02.710
in an ancient underground sanctuary on Windermere.

00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:06.520
That was Major Wright Immelmann.

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:13.430
We do not know how, but that fragment fell into the hands of Lady M.

00:06:13.650 --> 00:06:15.880
And that's how Mikumo came to be?

00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:16.670
Indeed.

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:21.480
When the Protoculture systems react to the Star Singer,

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:27.690
the brainwaves of humanoids synchronize on the delta wave level, forming a giant neural network.

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:30.160
Delta waves?

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:31.550
Correct.

00:06:31.550 --> 00:06:34.290
The waves of deep sleep and unconsciousness.

00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:37.370
In a way, the closest to death one can get.

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:42.890
There is a risk that those affected can't handle the gargantuan incoming information load

00:06:42.890 --> 00:06:45.550
and lose their sense of self as a result.

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:49.880
When that song is played, all races are at risk.

00:06:50.630 --> 00:06:52.680
Songs are a weapon.

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:56.060
It was just as I thought.

00:06:57.690 --> 00:07:03.310
The legend says the Star Singer lives to sing,

00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:09.240
and only those of or close to the royal house of Windermere can control it.

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:12.600
If Mikumo falls under the control of the enemy...

00:07:12.600 --> 00:07:13.740
If that happens...

00:07:14.150 --> 00:07:17.740
Then I will not guarantee her safety.

00:07:18.550 --> 00:07:19.860
No!

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:24.440
Atop the system on Ragna, the stage for the Star Singer,

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:26.380
the Star Shrine, has appeared.

00:07:27.430 --> 00:07:31.550
It will make the song of the stars resonate throughout the entire galaxy.

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:33.470
At its full power, that is.

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:35.360
But why is it on Ragna?

00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:39.070
Windermere and Ragna are on opposite sides of the globular cluster.

00:07:39.070 --> 00:07:40.560
Wind and sea.

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:43.500
Unless both are ready, it will not operate.

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:46.560
'Tis a safeguard of sorts.

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:49.440
Will you conquer the galaxy with that woman's song?

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:52.380
Only His Majesty can order her.

00:07:52.380 --> 00:07:57.020
His Majesty's song of the wind is what awakens the Star Singer's powers.

00:07:57.020 --> 00:08:00.080
Control of her is once again in Windermerean hands.

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:03.240
That song is dangerous.

00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:07.790
That is why the Protoculture gave us our runes.

00:08:08.390 --> 00:08:12.880
Our resistance to the song of the stars is stronger than other humanoids.

00:08:13.170 --> 00:08:15.640
The song of the wind is what they should hear!

00:08:16.840 --> 00:08:18.260
Obey Roid.

00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:19.260
Your Majesty!

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:22.730
Your Majesty, what are you...

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:28.220
Your Majesty?

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:36.900
I will sing as long as my rune lasts.

00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:38.760
I want you to obey Roid.

00:08:38.760 --> 00:08:41.080
Your lives should be in his hands.

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:42.290
As you wish.

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:51.380
I'm sorry, Keith.

00:08:51.960 --> 00:08:56.890
I couldn't tell you about the Star 
Singer before I knew for sure.

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:01.460
Lord Roid.

00:09:02.280 --> 00:09:03.230
What?

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:07.060
A NUNS fleet has infiltrated the Starwind sector.

00:09:07.430 --> 00:09:09.020
A NUNS fleet?

00:09:09.620 --> 00:09:15.160
They issued a warning to all civilian vessels to stay away from the globular cluster.

00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:17.310
They will use dimensional weapons.

00:09:17.310 --> 00:09:18.160
What?!

00:09:18.900 --> 00:09:22.660
Message from all units: all dimensional weapons loaded and ready.

00:09:23.240 --> 00:09:25.580
Ready to launch on arrival.

00:09:27.970 --> 00:09:28.880
What's going on?!

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:34.420
We informed NUNS that the Starwind sector is collapsing.

00:09:35.150 --> 00:09:38.570
And in exchange, you got the intel on Wright Immelmann?

00:09:38.570 --> 00:09:40.050
Why would you do this?

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:47.420
Most of our Foundation's investment on Windermere won't see any returns.

00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:49.750
My personal status is at risk as well.

00:09:50.640 --> 00:09:55.030
However, there is a chance to recoup this loss as long as the galaxy survives.

00:09:55.770 --> 00:09:58.380
I am a merchant.

00:09:58.380 --> 00:10:01.740
Even if it's just a single drop of blood, I won't give it away for free.

00:10:02.090 --> 00:10:04.240
But what about the dimensional weapons?!

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:09.540
I imagine they will announce that the Protoculture systems went haywire.

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:10.650
No way...

00:10:11.130 --> 00:10:13.500
Unexperienced youngsters.

00:10:14.120 --> 00:10:17.360
Attack will commence in two hours, at 1800.

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:19.510
Captain, message from Lady M.

00:10:20.210 --> 00:10:23.440
She predicts that the Windermereans will attack Ragna.

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:29.390
We are to immediately head to Ragna and repel their attack before the NUNS assault begins.

00:10:29.390 --> 00:10:32.090
Ignore NUNS and head to Ragna?

00:10:32.090 --> 00:10:32.770
But why?

00:10:33.610 --> 00:10:36.700
Well played, Lady M.

00:10:36.700 --> 00:10:38.490
Seems like you know some more.

00:10:39.500 --> 00:10:41.980
We'll have you share that later.

00:10:41.980 --> 00:10:43.450
All personnel, prepare for combat.

00:10:43.850 --> 00:10:45.600
We are heading to Ragna.

00:10:46.490 --> 00:10:48.010
Berger?

00:10:48.010 --> 00:10:49.120
You are too late.

00:10:50.170 --> 00:10:54.840
Lord Roid, even with the Protoculture systems, we cannot take a dimensional weapon attack head on!

00:10:55.990 --> 00:10:58.160
Nothing has changed in seven years.

00:10:58.870 --> 00:11:03.950
If it is for their benefit, they will not hesitate to taint the fatherland.

00:11:03.950 --> 00:11:06.930
They will erase all that does not fit with their intentions.

00:11:08.310 --> 00:11:11.240
Our wings shall put an end to this chain of evil.

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:15.320
Roid, I leave the Star Singer to you.

00:11:15.320 --> 00:11:16.020
Your Majesty!

00:11:16.330 --> 00:11:18.580
Keith, the Knights are in your hands.

00:11:18.580 --> 00:11:19.360
Your Majesty!

00:11:19.760 --> 00:11:24.820
The humanoids of the galaxy shall be free from the rule of the UN Government.

00:11:24.820 --> 00:11:26.830
May the winds of freedom blow!

00:11:27.430 --> 00:11:29.530
For the Great Wind!

00:11:37.680 --> 00:11:40.930
I do not approve of your way of doing things.

00:11:40.930 --> 00:11:43.510
I suspect you are still hiding something.

00:11:44.070 --> 00:11:47.680
But at least I feel no lies in your rune.

00:11:53.900 --> 00:11:57.690
Do you remember the first time we flew?

00:12:00.510 --> 00:12:05.280
We raced to see who could fly the highest and fastest.

00:12:11.970 --> 00:12:13.900
I won.

00:12:14.740 --> 00:12:17.700
That moment felt like an eternity to me.

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:22.600
I felt that my soul and these skies would last forever.

00:12:24.550 --> 00:12:26.830
I still remember it.

00:12:27.510 --> 00:12:32.980
I want eternal peace for the galaxy, built around Windermere and His Majesty.

00:12:34.070 --> 00:12:35.900
I don't care about the galaxy.

00:12:36.950 --> 00:12:44.000
As long as I can protect these skies, I don't care if my soul burns up in a flash either.

00:12:50.020 --> 00:12:51.130
I know.

00:12:52.700 --> 00:12:54.670
For these skies.

00:12:59.530 --> 00:13:01.040
Makina...

00:13:01.040 --> 00:13:04.670
I'm fine. You should go, Fre-Fre.

00:13:06.460 --> 00:13:08.640
I'll stay a little longer.

00:13:09.610 --> 00:13:11.560
Gotcha. Take care, then.

00:13:20.620 --> 00:13:23.340
What are you doing, Freyja?

00:13:23.340 --> 00:13:25.650
Nothing, really.

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:28.680
Is that wound not healed yet?

00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:37.900
I was born into a family who has been in charge of this sanctum since ancient times.

00:13:37.900 --> 00:13:42.210
The first story of the Protoculture I heard was the legend of the Star Singer.

00:13:42.850 --> 00:13:46.010
I have been obsessed with their 
culture and civilization ever since,

00:13:46.010 --> 00:13:47.680
so I kept researching.

00:13:48.360 --> 00:13:53.400
However, uncovering all the mysteries demands more time than our fleeting lives grants us.

00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:55.510
At least that's how I used to think.

00:13:56.320 --> 00:14:00.250
But your light made me think otherwise.

00:14:03.070 --> 00:14:04.610
Star Shrine?

00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:08.600
That thing appeared on Ragna, and that's why the Windermereans are heading there?

00:14:08.600 --> 00:14:09.360
Yes.

00:14:09.670 --> 00:14:13.580
Ragna is a place where gates 
to subspace are easier to open.

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:17.330
I suspect that is somehow related.

00:14:18.010 --> 00:14:20.360
There are other rumors as well.

00:14:20.360 --> 00:14:26.090
They say that at the end of the Vajra War, Chaos intercepted a transmission from subspace.

00:14:26.750 --> 00:14:33.410
Its frequency was the same as that of the 1st Long Distance Colonization Fleet's flagship

00:14:33.410 --> 00:14:38.270
the Megaroad-01, that went missing fifty years earlier.

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:44.230
TL Note: Lynn Minmay

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:44.230
I hear that the person called Lady M made their debut around that time as well.

00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:47.990
Ah, forgive my idle banter.

00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:52.680
I pray for your victory.

00:14:55.810 --> 00:14:58.060
What can we do about the gear from Epsilon?

00:14:58.060 --> 00:15:02.770
Replacing it all will take ten years' worth of our budget.

00:15:02.770 --> 00:15:05.880
I don't mind taking a temporary pay cut if it means we can get rid of it.

00:15:06.320 --> 00:15:08.810
We're off to the final battle. On Ragna.

00:15:08.810 --> 00:15:11.040
Walküre isn't ready for it though.

00:15:11.040 --> 00:15:12.390
We'll pull it off.

00:15:13.340 --> 00:15:14.800
I have a dream.

00:15:14.800 --> 00:15:15.870
A dream?

00:15:16.660 --> 00:15:20.430
Walküre... All of us singing the songs we love.

00:15:20.430 --> 00:15:24.480
Makina, Reina, Freyja, Mikumo, and I.

00:15:25.460 --> 00:15:27.850
No war, no Var.

00:15:27.850 --> 00:15:29.450
Just us singing to our hearts' content.

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:32.100
I won't mind if it's just a small stage.

00:15:33.680 --> 00:15:35.340
I take that back.

00:15:35.340 --> 00:15:40.470
I want our songs to reach the entire galaxy.

00:15:41.530 --> 00:15:42.840
I understand.

00:15:42.840 --> 00:15:45.380
I want to get over with this war

00:15:45.820 --> 00:15:49.480
and let Hayate, Mirage, and Chuck fly as they wish.

00:15:50.510 --> 00:15:53.620
Let's make those dreams come true.

00:15:53.620 --> 00:15:55.270
Let's all make it back.

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:19.740
I'll take back Ragna and Marianne.

00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:26.540
Your unit's good as new, Lieutenant.

00:16:27.250 --> 00:16:32.050
Messer's plane needed some fixing due to all the overdrive.

00:16:32.270 --> 00:16:33.790
Thanks.

00:16:33.790 --> 00:16:35.050
Second Lt. Hayate!

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:38.220
I'm glad the truth about your father came out.

00:16:38.540 --> 00:16:40.460
Yeah, thanks.

00:16:41.220 --> 00:16:43.980
When they talked about my dad on Windermere,

00:16:43.980 --> 00:16:48.360
it made me really happy when you said no one really knows the truth.

00:16:48.670 --> 00:16:49.860
I've got your back.

00:16:52.450 --> 00:16:53.290
What's wrong?

00:16:55.240 --> 00:16:57.070
You should go see Freyja.

00:16:59.230 --> 00:17:01.360
We're heading to the final battle.

00:17:01.360 --> 00:17:03.720
I'll call you if there is an emergency sortie.

00:17:04.730 --> 00:17:05.690
Mirage...

00:17:07.110 --> 00:17:07.960
Thanks!

00:17:09.450 --> 00:17:10.140
You're welcome.

00:17:13.410 --> 00:17:14.510
I'll be back.

00:17:16.840 --> 00:17:18.360
Hayate?

00:17:18.360 --> 00:17:20.460
Kaname, where's Freyja?

00:17:20.460 --> 00:17:21.720
She's not here.

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:23.110
Thanks!

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:25.610
Fre-Fre?

00:17:25.610 --> 00:17:27.580
She left not too long ago.

00:17:28.420 --> 00:17:30.230
Thanks. Get well soon!

00:17:35.700 --> 00:17:37.200
Why won't she answer?

00:17:44.500 --> 00:17:45.500
Freyja...

00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:46.860
Hayate.

00:17:46.860 --> 00:17:49.850
What were you doing? I've been calling you.

00:17:49.850 --> 00:17:52.840
Huh? Ah, my battery ran out!

00:17:52.840 --> 00:17:53.860
Goodness...

00:17:53.860 --> 00:17:54.680
Sorry.

00:17:54.680 --> 00:17:58.020
Should you really be here before such a big operation?

00:17:58.970 --> 00:18:01.180
I guess not, huh?

00:18:01.610 --> 00:18:03.560
You should go and prepare.

00:18:04.380 --> 00:18:05.480
Freyja?

00:18:06.130 --> 00:18:07.830
Let's do our best.

00:18:09.030 --> 00:18:10.770
There you are, Second Lt. Hayate!

00:18:12.900 --> 00:18:13.690
Here you go.

00:18:14.080 --> 00:18:16.620
Do you know how long I've been looking for you?

00:18:16.620 --> 00:18:19.160
Sorry. What is it?

00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:20.820
It's from your mother.

00:18:22.020 --> 00:18:26.580
It seems it went around the entire galaxy before it finally got here.

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:29.260
I'm glad you got it before your sortie.

00:18:31.150 --> 00:18:33.500
Is it okay for you to open it with me here?

00:18:33.780 --> 00:18:35.380
I don't mind.

00:18:37.580 --> 00:18:38.720
What's that?

00:18:39.690 --> 00:18:42.180
The letters and stuff my dad sent me.

00:18:43.660 --> 00:18:46.120
I told her I became a pilot.

00:18:46.120 --> 00:18:51.150
I figure this is her answer to me going down the same path as my dad.

00:18:51.150 --> 00:18:52.650
Can I see?

00:18:52.650 --> 00:18:53.420
Sure.

00:18:57.630 --> 00:18:58.820
So pretty.

00:18:59.230 --> 00:19:02.420
Dad was a special agent, huh...

00:19:02.420 --> 00:19:05.240
He might've picked this up in some ancient ruin too.

00:19:11.450 --> 00:19:15.670
Is this you and your dad?

00:19:32.100 --> 00:19:33.130
What's wrong?

00:19:33.640 --> 00:19:35.410
I'll tell you later.

00:19:37.400 --> 00:19:38.190
Look.

00:19:40.250 --> 00:19:41.530
His letters?

00:19:41.810 --> 00:19:43.940
They're all one sentence.

00:19:46.900 --> 00:19:48.460
The sky is vast.

00:19:49.850 --> 00:19:51.450
The stars are many.

00:19:52.280 --> 00:19:53.960
The scent of rain.

00:19:54.820 --> 00:19:56.420
The sea is blue.

00:19:57.890 --> 00:20:00.250
The desert is hot.

00:20:00.250 --> 00:20:02.130
The snow makes my teeth ache.

00:20:03.490 --> 00:20:06.120
Walking on the sand with bare feet.

00:20:06.120 --> 00:20:08.600
The trees rustle in the wind.

00:20:09.460 --> 00:20:10.630
The galaxy...

00:20:12.080 --> 00:20:13.880
The galaxy's huge.

00:20:22.570 --> 00:20:27.000
Your father was trying to protect everyone.

00:20:28.150 --> 00:20:29.430
I'll do it.

00:20:30.790 --> 00:20:34.920
I'll protect you, your home, and Ragna too.

00:20:37.140 --> 00:20:38.800
Might as well throw the entire galaxy in.

00:20:47.290 --> 00:20:48.470
I like this.

00:20:51.110 --> 00:20:54.050
The way you laugh makes me feel relieved.

00:21:36.420 --> 00:21:40.820
Mission 25: Star Singer

00:21:43.240 --> 00:21:44.780
Is it really possible?

00:21:45.400 --> 00:21:49.600
While this sanctuary is smaller than the one that appeared on Ragna,

00:21:49.600 --> 00:21:51.740
they should work in a similar fashion.

00:21:53.410 --> 00:21:56.000
The foe is already in the globular cluster.

00:21:56.580 --> 00:21:58.670
We must act quickly.

00:21:59.610 --> 00:22:02.550
Please give the order, Your Majesty.

00:22:06.110 --> 00:22:08.590
As the true king, I command you!

00:22:09.830 --> 00:22:11.800
Rudanjal Rom Mayan!

00:22:14.220 --> 00:22:15.460
No!

00:22:28.320 --> 00:22:29.850
This voice...

00:22:29.850 --> 00:22:30.740
So sharp.

00:22:33.560 --> 00:22:34.910
Mikumo?

00:22:34.910 --> 00:22:37.470
Fold jamming decreasing!

00:22:37.470 --> 00:22:39.170
Currently 17%!

00:22:40.060 --> 00:22:42.120
Is it the song of the wind?

00:22:42.120 --> 00:22:43.380
What about the dimensional weapons?

00:23:25.920 --> 00:23:29.700
This is the power of the song of the stars.

00:23:36.810 --> 00:23:39.810
Next time: Eternal Walkure

00:23:39.810 --> 00:23:39.860
supposedly after Subaru wakes up and has his confession scene with Emilia, "we" find out that Rem and Crusch's party encountered some other sin archbishops and got wrecked. 
